  "body": "When [setting document.domain](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction), the spec says:\r\n> If _host_ equals _host_'s public suffix, then return false. [URL]\r\n\r\nbut it should say\r\n\r\n_If _host_ is a suffix of _host_'s public suffix, then return false. [URL]_,\r\n\r\nFor example, if dyndns.example.com.cc and com.cc are in the public suffix list, a domain such as customer1.dyndns.example.com.cc should not be able to set its `document.domain` to any of `dyndns.example.com.cc`, `example.com.cc`, `com.cc` nor `cc`.",
